{
  "query": "Skyline Air operates a hybrid platform and needs a fully managed database in Google Cloud while several legacy reservation services must continue on dedicated bare metal systems in its colocation site. The link between the legacy tier and the cloud database must stay within the same metro and deliver under 8 millisecond round trip latency, and the business requires strong transactional consistency with straightforward operations. Which combination of Google services best satisfies these needs?",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL and Google Bare Metal Solution",
      "explanation": "This pairing combines a managed PostgreSQL database with dedicated bare metal hosted adjacent to Google Cloud for legacy workloads",
      "correct": false,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Cloud Spanner and Google Bare Metal Solution",
      "explanation": "This option pairs a strongly consistent horizontally scalable relational database with dedicated bare metal in a Google operated facility connected with low latency",
      "correct": true,
      "selected": false
    },
    {
      "text": "AlloyDB for PostgreSQL and Google Anthos Bare Metal",
      "explanation": "This combination uses a high performance PostgreSQL compatible service alongside Kubernetes clusters running on customer owned servers",
      "correct": false,
