  ],
  "answer": "<p>The correct option is <b>Cloud Spanner and Google Bare Metal Solution</b>.</p><p>Cloud Spanner provides a fully managed relational database with external strong consistency, high availability, and automatic scaling. It delivers transactional guarantees that suit reservation systems and keeps operations straightforward since Google manages maintenance, replication, backups, and failover. A regional Spanner deployment can keep commit latency low while still providing synchronous replication across zones for resilience.</p><p>Google Bare Metal Solution places dedicated servers in facilities adjacent to Google Cloud regions within the same metro and connects them to Google Cloud with high throughput and very low latency links. This lets the legacy reservation services remain on dedicated bare metal while maintaining round trip times in the single digit millisecond range to the managed database, which satisfies the under eight millisecond latency requirement.</p><p><i>Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL and Google Bare Metal Solution</i> is less suitable for a large scale reservation platform because Cloud SQL does not provide the same external consistency model and horizontal scalability as Spanner. Meeting high and variable throughput would likely require sharding and more operational work, which conflicts with the goal of straightforward operations.</p><p><i>AlloyDB for PostgreSQL and Google Anthos Bare Metal</i> does not meet the requirement for dedicated bare metal provided as a managed service in the same metro because Anthos Bare Metal is a Kubernetes platform that runs on customer supplied hardware rather than a hosted bare metal offering. AlloyDB also does not provide the same externally consistent transactions at massive scale that Spanner offers.</p><p><i>Cloud Bigtable and Google Distributed Cloud Hosted</i> is not appropriate because Bigtable is a NoSQL wide column store without full relational transactions and ACID semantics, which conflicts with the need for strong transactional consistency. Google Distributed Cloud Hosted is designed for disconnected or highly restricted environments and does not target the metro connected colocation pattern described.</p>",
